  "ai_summary": "Consultancy stocks collapsed 24% this month (down 35% YoY), as investors price in AI replacing low-value work. Amazon\u2019s 14,000 recent cuts drove a 6.6% YoY Big Tech decline, signaling AI-driven labor reductions. Indeed postings dipped 1.6% lately despite 11% YoY growth, a leading indicator of cooling intent. Stagnant monthly hiring at AI labs follows massive yearly gains. The market is pivoting sharply from generalists to AI specialists. If you aren't an AI specialist, your resume is currently being used as training data for the bot that's going to replace you.",
